  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In Southern Border, Duke Long drives Heaven Overseeing Tower to burst with intense white light when Zuo Ye Hui charges the tower. The strike is Fate Vanquish, tied to rank nine Immortal Gu Fate; there is no way of dodging, and anyone below rank nine loses to the move. Gu Immortals exposed to the light, righteous or demonic, cough blood, suffer heavy injury, and most faint, clearing half the battlefield, while some shielded by dream realms are spared. Zuo Ye Hui is hit and crashes down but does not die, and Fairy Zi Wei notes that the tower cannot use the move consecutively while Fate Gu still has injuries.",
      "chapters": [
        1359
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_duke_long",
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower",
        "char_zuo_ye_hui",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_fate_gu",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heaven Overseeing Tower uses Fate Vanquish again later in that Southern Border fighting.",
      "chapters": [
        1366
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "southern-border-recast",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the later Heavenly Court battle the move is again named Immortal killer move Fate Vanquish.",
      "chapters": [
        1742
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-naming",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heaven Overseeing Tower unleashes rank nine immortal killer move Fate Vanquish, and Fang Yuan is shocked that the reuse interval has shortened so far. Several Immortal Gu Houses on his side are completely destroyed with the Gu Immortals inside; of two rank eight Gu Immortals behind him, one is near death and the other unconscious, and the rest are badly injured. Observers contrast the terror with Southern Border’s earlier weaker showing and blame a complete rank nine Fate Gu. Fang Yuan alone does not fall; he is a complete otherworldly demon to whom Fate Vanquish is like harmless light.",
      "chapters": [
        1744
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-nine-volley",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At a later crisis Heaven Overseeing Tower activates Fate Vanquish again and instantly kills over half of the Gu Immortals on Fang Yuan’s side, while only Fang Yuan is immune.",
      "chapters": [
        1748
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "crisis-volley",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal killer move Fate Vanquish is used again; Fang Yuan is a complete otherworldly demon who cannot be targeted by it and has natural immunity. The killer move Fate Vanquish with Fate Gu as the core has no effect on him. Allied Gu Immortals warn each other to be careful of Heaven Overseeing Tower, especially Fate Vanquish, and ask after Fang Yuan as the only one who can resist it.",
      "chapters": [
        1953
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-gu-core",
